  "_commit": {
    "id": "1f49dedc0282c76784ac0f996cb6ae9716e2ae45",
    "author": "Patrick Aboyoun <aboyoun.patrick@gene.com>",
    "committer": "Patrick Aboyoun <aboyoun.patrick@gene.com>",
    "message": "Implement bindROWS for row-number-keyed DuckDBTable\n\nBacks rbind() via BiocGenerics::rbind's RectangularData dispatch,\npreviously an unconditional stop(). A user asked whether rbind()/c()\nnot being supported was a deliberate choice and drafted a candidate\nimplementation around dbplyr::bind_queries() (UNION ALL).\n\nIt was deliberate for tables with real, named keycols: row identity\nunder a named key has no well-defined union across tables, so that\ncase still errors, now naming the offending keycols. For the common\nrow-number-keyed case (the default construction), each side's pending\ndatacols transformations are resolved via tblconn() before the union\nrather than the raw @conn, tables with different columns are\nsupported (missing columns NULL-filled, as dplyr::bind_rows() does),\nand a fresh row-number key is computed afterward.\n",
    "time": 1793425280
  },
